<template>
<!-- 10. WebSockets & SSE -->
<section id="websockets" class="docs-section">
  <h2>10. WebSockets & SSE</h2>
  <p>Zenith exposes WebSocket upgrades through <code>upgrade_websocket(req)</code>. The returned value reads and writes frames over the active HTTP connection, including its TLS layer under <code>listen_tls()</code>.</p>
  <p>Each live handler is a cooperative task, so it calls <code>task.yield()</code> when a non-blocking read has no complete message. Capacity depends on workload and deployment; Zenith does not create one OS thread per socket.</p>

  <CodeEditor title="websockets.vn" lines="19">
    app.<span class="token-function">get</span>(<span class="token-string">"/chat"</span>, |req| \{
    <span class="token-keyword">let</span> ws <span class="token-keyword">=</span> <span class="token-function">upgrade_websocket</span>(req)
    <span class="token-keyword">if</span> ws == <span class="token-keyword">null</span> \{ <span class="token-keyword">return</span> Response \{ status: 426, body: <span class="token-string">"upgrade required"</span>, content_type: <span class="token-string">"text/plain"</span> \} \}
    <span class="token-keyword">while</span> <span class="token-keyword">true</span> \{
      <span class="token-keyword">let</span> message_text <span class="token-keyword">=</span> ws.<span class="token-function">read</span>()
      <span class="token-keyword">if</span> message_text == <span class="token-keyword">null</span> \{ <span class="token-keyword">break</span> \}
      <span class="token-keyword">if</span> message_text != <span class="token-string">""</span> \{ ws.<span class="token-function">write</span>(message_text) \}
      task.<span class="token-function">yield</span>()
    \}
    <span class="token-keyword">return</span> http.<span class="token-function">create_struct</span>([<span class="token-string">"_keep_open"</span>], [<span class="token-keyword">true</span>])
    \})
  </CodeEditor>
</section>

<!-- 11. Background Job Workers -->
<section id="queues" class="docs-section">
  <h2>11. Background Job Workers</h2>
  <p>Varian includes a local SQLite-backed job queue for work that should outlive an HTTP response. Named jobs persist in the <code>vn_jobs</code> table; cooperative worker tasks poll and execute their registered handlers.</p>
  <p>The built-in queue is process-local orchestration over one SQLite database, not a Redis or distributed queue. Use an external broker when several machines must claim jobs from one shared queue.</p>

  <CodeEditor title="queue.vn" lines="27">
    <span class="token-keyword">let</span> app <span class="token-keyword">=</span> <span class="token-function">new_app</span>()
    <span class="token-function">queue_configure</span>(<span class="token-string">"varian-jobs.db"</span>, 3)

    <span class="token-comment">// Register the named handler before starting workers.</span>
    <span class="token-function">queue_register_job</span>(<span class="token-string">"transcode_video"</span>, |payload| \{
      <span class="token-keyword">let</span> job = <span class="token-function">json_decode</span>(payload)
      python.<span class="token-function">run</span>(<span class="token-string">"video_tools"</span>, <span class="token-string">"transcode"</span>, [job.video_id, job.target_resolution])
    \})

    <span class="token-keyword">let</span> pool = <span class="token-function">new_worker_pool</span>()
    pool.<span class="token-function">spawn</span>(3)

    <span class="token-comment">// Persist a named job from a request handler.</span>
    app.<span class="token-function">post</span>(<span class="token-string">"/api/video/process"</span>, |req| \{
    <span class="token-keyword">let</span> params <span class="token-keyword">=</span> <span class="token-function">json_decode</span>(req.body)
    <span class="token-function">queue_submit_job</span>(<span class="token-string">"transcode_video"</span>, <span class="token-function">json_encode</span>(\{
      video_id: params.video_id, target_resolution: <span class="token-string">"1080p"</span>
    \}))
    <span class="token-keyword">return</span> <span class="token-function">json_response</span>(\{ task_status: <span class="token-string">"queued"</span> \}, <span class="token-number">202</span>)
    \}, <span class="token-string">"Enqueue video job"</span>)
  </CodeEditor>

  <div class="hint-box">
    <h4>💡 Hint: Scalability Model</h4>
    <p>Workers are cooperative Varian tasks inside one process; they are not OS threads. Named jobs are durable in SQLite, while <code>pool.submit(closure)</code> stores the closure only in memory and therefore is not restart-safe.</p>
  </div>
</section>
</template>

